## Where Work Happens

This is the critical part — **who does what:**

| Work | Where | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Event logging (MongoDB write) | **Node.js** | EventBus + Mongoose live here |
| Queue enqueue | **Node.js** → **Redis** | BullMQ producer is in Node.js |
| Page building trigger (check ≥20) | **Node.js** (RAG Worker) | Reads MongoDB, decision logic |
| Page summarization (LLM) | **Node.js** ⚠️ | `ragService.buildPages()` calls Mistral via Langchain |
| Text embedding (1024-dim vector) | **Python RAG-Service** | `POST /pages/embed` → Mistral embed |
| Pinecone upsert | **Python RAG-Service** | Same endpoint |
| Semantic search | **Python RAG-Service** | `POST /search` → embed query → Pinecone |
| Chat LLM response | **Python RAG-Service** | `POST /chat` → prompt assembly → Mistral LLM |
| Chat history summarization | **Python RAG-Service** | `POST /history/summarize` → Mistral |
| WebSocket notification | **Node.js** (Notification Worker) | Socket.io lives in Node.js |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **The split is uneven.** Page summarization (the heaviest CPU-bound Node.js work) uses Langchain's `ChatMistralAI` directly from Node.js, while the embedding/search/chat all go through the Python RAG-Service. In a fully decoupled architecture, this summarization should also move to the RAG-Service.

